1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,940
What if the Moon vanished tonight?
Imagine it disappears without debris
or an explosion.

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:10,550
Earth would keep spinning. Losing
the Moon would not suddenly switch
off gravity or stop our orbit.

3
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:15,780
Ocean tides would change, but they
would not disappear. The Sun also
pulls on the oceans.

4
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:21,040
Nights without moonlight would look
darker, changing a familiar cue for
many living things.

5
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:27,265
The Moon helps stabilize our axial
tilt. Any long term consequences
would need careful modeling.

6
00:00:27,265 --> 00:00:33,375
So the first surprise is not instant
chaos. It is a missing light,
followed by a changed world.
